# Test: the admin form for `system command help` renders its name input and
# posts the typed command name through the daemon
# VALIDATES: the `help` container of ze-system-cmd.yang
# (internal/core/ipc/yang/ze-system-cmd.yang) declares the `name` leaf under
# its ze:command container, which is the one declaration extractArgDefs
# (internal/component/config/yang/command.go) reads into the node's ArgDefs,
# so the page renders one input carrying the leaf's two texts, and the value
# typed into it reaches the command the web server dispatches: the result
# card's title is `system command help name list`, keyword before value, and
# its body is the dispatcher's answer. The value is one word because a `.wb`
# text needle carries no quotes, and a value holding a space is quoted in the
# title (writeArgumentValue, internal/component/web/handler_admin.go).
# PREVENTS: the leaf living on the rpc input of ze-system-api.yang alone, which
# the command tree never reads, so the page renders NO input and Execute posts
# the bare `system command help`, which the daemon refuses with its usage line
# (plan/journal/command-takes-an-untyped-positional-value.md, 2026-09-15).
# The web suite starts `ze start --web-only`, whose dispatcher
# (webOnlyDispatcher, cmd/ze/hub/service_web.go) answers every operational
# command with the standalone-mode message, so the answer the card carries is
# that message: it proves the POST reached the dispatcher and the title proves
# what the dispatcher was handed. The daemon's own answer to both forms is
# TestCommandHelpAnswersTheKeywordForm
# (internal/component/plugin/server/command_help_argument_test.go).

option=timeout:value=30s

action=open:path=/admin/system/command/help
expect=element:text=system command help
expect=element:text=Command name
expect=element:text=as command list prints it
action=fill:id=param-name:value=list
action=click:text=Execute
expect=element:text=system command help name list
expect=element:text=running in standalone mode
expect=element:not-text=panic
